# Line endings that matter.
#
# Nothing here is cosmetic: these files are executed inside Linux images. On a
# Windows checkout without `core.autocrlf=false`, git hands the build context a
# CRLF copy, and busybox `sh` fails on the carriage return:
#
#   /app/start.sh: line 2: : not found
#   /app/start.sh: line 31: syntax error: unexpected end of file
#
# The image then restarts forever and the stack comes up "unhealthy".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Python/CLI shims with a shebang, executed on Linux.
apps/api/bin/* text eol=lf
